    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0733" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg627"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ecuadorean
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-28"><hi rendition="#italic">May 28,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm the
                    conversation which took place between us to-day in respect of the desirability
                    of united effort on the part of the authorities of the United States who are now
                    charged with the sanitary work in the city of Panama and in the Canal Zone of
                    the Isthmus, and the authorities of Ecuador, for the more perfect reciprocal
                    protection of each against contagious and epidemic diseases.</p>
                <p>It will give the authorities of the United States very great pleasure to unite in
                    friendly cooperation with the authorities of Ecuador to this mutually beneficial
                    end to carry out the suggestion.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
